<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main" class="container narrow-container">
  <section class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE ABOUT QUIZFORGE</span><h1>Built for the<br><span class="accent-text">“wait, I know this!”</span></h1><p class="hero-description">A small trivia app with a simple idea: a few good questions can make any day a little more interesting.</p></section>
  <section class="panel about-panel"><span class="step-label">01</span><h2>One round. Three simple steps.</h2><ol class="about-steps"><li><strong>Make it yours.</strong> Choose a category, difficulty, and either 5 or 10 questions.</li><li><strong>Give it a go.</strong> Pick one answer for every question. You can change your mind before submitting.</li><li><strong>Learn something.</strong> Get your score and review every correct answer. Start another round whenever you’re ready.</li></ol></section>
  <section class="panel about-panel"><span class="step-label">02</span><h2>Real questions, thoughtfully handled.</h2><p>Questions and categories come from <a href="https://opentdb.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Trivia Database</a>, a free, community-contributed question bank. Questions are in English, and availability depends on the category and difficulty you choose.</p><p>Answer choices are shuffled on the server. Correct answers stay in your server session until you submit. Your result is the number of correct answers divided by the number of questions, rounded to a whole percentage.</p><p>OpenTDB limits question requests to one per IP address every five seconds. If it needs a breather, QuizForge will let you know. A browser session keeps only your current round and latest result; restarting the server clears them.</p></section>
  <section class="panel about-panel"><span class="step-label">03</span><h2>Made to learn. Made to share.</h2><p>QuizForge is an individual Web Development II project, built with Node.js, Express, Axios, EJS, dotenv, and express-session.</p><p>Trivia content is provided by Open Trivia DB under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0</a>. QuizForge presents the questions with shuffled answer choices and an answer review. The interface illustrations are custom SVGs created for this project.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://opentdb.com/api_config.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the API documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <div class="bottom-cta"><h2>Ready to test that curious mind?</h2><a class="button button-primary" href="/">Let’s play <%- include('partials/icon', { name: 'arrow-right' }) %></a></div>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
